{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_05_the_prototype_chain_02_prototype_vs_the_slot_prototype_vs_internal_slot", "label": "prototype vs [[Prototype]]", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/05-the-prototype-chain/02-prototype-vs-the-slot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "[[Prototype]] is an internal slot on every object. Fn.prototype is an ordinary property only functions have, the object new will install. A function's own prototype is Function.prototype."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_05_the_prototype_chain_02_prototype_vs_the_slot_new_operator", "label": "What new actually does", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/05-the-prototype-chain/02-prototype-vs-the-slot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Creates a fresh object whose [[Prototype]] is Fn.prototype, calls Fn with this bound to it, and returns it. No methods are copied; instances share one function object."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_05_the_prototype_chain_02_prototype_vs_the_slot_constructor_property", "label": "constructor back-reference", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/05-the-prototype-chain/02-prototype-vs-the-slot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An own property of Fn.prototype pointing back at Fn. Replacing prototype wholesale discards it. Writable and forgeable \u2014 never use it for type checks."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_05_the_prototype_chain_02_prototype_vs_the_slot_object_create", "label": "Object.create", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/05-the-prototype-chain/02-prototype-vs-the-slot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sets [[Prototype]] directly with no constructor call. Descriptor defaults are all false. Object.create(null) gives no chain at all."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_05_the_prototype_chain_02_prototype_vs_the_slot_class_is_same_machinery", "label": "class is the same lookup machinery", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/05-the-prototype-chain/02-prototype-vs-the-slot.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Class methods go on Ctor.prototype. class adds private fields, extends wiring, strict bodies, non-enumerable methods and a constructor that throws without new."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_05_the_prototype_chain_02_prototype_vs_the_slot_new_operator", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_05_the_prototype_chain_02_prototype_vs_the_slot_prototype_vs_internal_slot", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/05-the-prototype-chain/02-prototype-vs-the-slot.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_05_the_prototype_chain_02_prototype_vs_the_slot_class_is_same_machinery", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_05_the_prototype_chain_02_prototype_vs_the_slot_new_operator", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/05-the-prototype-chain/02-prototype-vs-the-slot.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source"